As the sun beat down on the dusty roads of Stranglethorn Vale, Glimble Sparkspanner, a diminutive Gnome Warlock, trudged along with his trusty Succubus, Xylara, by his side. They had been questing for hours, taking on the various tasks set by the local NPCs. Xylara, with her razor-sharp claws and mischievous grin, had proven to be a valuable asset in battle, taking down the numerous jungle creatures that dared to stand in their way.

As they approached the next quest objective, a group of vicious Raptor-like creatures, Glimble patted Xylara on the head, saying, "You're the best, Xylara! I don't know what I'd do without you!" Xylara meowed contentedly, her eyes gleaming with a malevolent light.

Now, about that answer...

The reason Warlocks are often seen with Voidwalkers instead of Succubi is because of the latter's ability to "Taunt" - a skill that makes them more likely to be attacked by mobs, drawing aggro away from the Warlock. This makes them more useful in solo play, but less desirable in group play, where the Warlock's own survivability is more important. [end of text]


